## Deploy code after local changes (CI — preferred)

**Do not rsync from the laptop by default.** Push to GitHub and use:

- Workflow: `.github/workflows/deploy-web.yml` (`Deploy web`)
- Auto: push to `main` / `master` / `release/**` when `timetrack/**` changes
- Manual: Actions → **Deploy web** → Run workflow
- Secret: `PRODUCTION_SSH_KEY` (same as client release)

### Manual laptop rsync (only if user explicitly asks)

Local repo: `/home/netadmin/networkadminn`. Sync **only** the `timetrack/` tree:

```bash
rsync -avz --delete \
  --exclude '__pycache__' --exclude '*.pyc' \
  -e "ssh -i ~/Documents/sachinsharma/server-key.pem -p 22 -o IdentitiesOnly=yes" \
  /home/netadmin/networkadminn/timetrack/ \
  root@31.97.239.250:/www/wwwroot/timetrack/timetrack/
```

Then reload workers (graceful):

```bash
ssh -i ~/Documents/sachinsharma/server-key.pem -p 22 -o IdentitiesOnly=yes root@31.97.239.250 \
  'kill -HUP $(cat /www/wwwroot/timetrack/gunicorn.pid)'
```

Verify a fix landed, e.g. `grep _apply_offline_overrides /www/wwwroot/timetrack/timetrack/analytics.py`.

## Not production

- `/opt/esstracker/` on the employee PC = **agent client** install only; updating it does **not** update the website.

